{
  "reviews": {
    "node-1pbq4gz": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims 'local indication P-R normally shows normal pressure band' as a condition supported by evidence. However, the provided excerpts (IA-P02) define P-R only as a point mapping to RHOB receiving header H-R and do not establish what constitutes a 'normal pressure band' or confirm that it was showing one at any specific time prior to 10:00 AM other than sampled values starting at 09:54. The claim relies on inference from context rather than explicit measurement in provided excerpts, which violates the requirement for direct evidence of the complete proposition.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Explicit record or excerpt stating that P-R normally shows a normal pressure band (defining 'normal') and confirming it was showing such at 09:54 AM prior to the drop. Alternatively, an excerpt defining the expected operating range for P-R under stable conditions.","question":"Does any supplied document define what constitutes a 'normal pressure band' for point P-R or confirm that P-R showed normal values immediately before 10:00 AM?"
    },
    "node-1dzzqd8": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node asserts no engineering disposition or temporary instruction was attached for changes to instrument-air service affecting RHOB between March and May. The evidence (IA-D03) states that if a change affects an existing boundary, the ECP must be revised OR have an approved temporary instruction attached; draft preparation alone does not satisfy distribution. However, there is no record confirming whether any such change actually occurred or was implemented for this case prior to incident. Claim remains proposed rule without confirmation of application here.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Record showing either: (1) a service-routing change affecting RHOB that required ECP revision/temporary instruction and evidence it was not done, OR (2) explicit statement that no such changes occurred in the period specified.","question":"Is there any record indicating whether a service-routing change to instrument-air supply affected RHOB between 2024-03-01 and May 20, 2024?"
    },
    "node-psncku": {
      "supported": false,
      "issue": "The node claims the work package cover indicates the temporary instruction attachment field was blank at issue time. While finding-1yf38nl supports that the field was indeed blank (status: supported), this node's label frames it as a condition about what the cover 'indicates' rather than an inference about service-routing status. The detail incorrectly attributes support from passage p2 which discusses training extracts not stating configuration drawings seen, conflating two separate claims.",
      "evidenceNeeded": "Direct excerpt from IA-S02_work_package_cover.md confirming WO-527-E field execution record was blank at folder issue time (already supported by finding-1yf38nl but misattributed here).","question":"Does the work package cover for WO-527 explicitly state that the temporary instruction attachment field is 'Blank at folder issue'?"
    }
  },
  "decision": {
    "summary": "All three nodes are unsupported due to lack of direct evidence supporting their complete propositions. Node node-psncku conflates a supported fact (blank field) with an unsupported inference about service-routing status; its label should reflect only the blank-field observation if that were intended, but as written it implies knowledge of routing changes which is unknown.",
    "evidenceUsed": ["finding-1yf38nl", "IA-D03_change_and_work_record_requirements.md excerpts"],
    "unknowns": [
      "Whether any service-routing change occurred affecting RHOB between March and May 2024",
      "What constitutes a 'normal pressure band' for P-R at the time of incident"
    ],
    "alternatives": [
      "The air interruption may have originated upstream (North gallery) or downstream without involving service-routing changes.",
      "A procedural gap exists in documenting routing changes, but no evidence confirms one occurred here."
    ],"confidence": 0.95 }
}
